  "body": {
    "id": "thm:verified-reconstruction-positive-answer",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Let \\(S\\) be a compact convex rational polygon, let \\(B\\) and the cells be\nrational polygonal, let every \\(\\mu_{dj}\\) have a rational piecewise-constant\ndensity, and let \\(d\\nu=w\\,d\\mathcal H^1\\), where \\(w\\) is nonnegative,\nnormalized, and rational piecewise affine on \\(B\\).  For rational \\(M_d\\ge0\\),\nrational \\(m_d\\in K_d\\) with \\(r_d(m_d)>0\\), and rational \\(\\epsilon>0\\), the\nanswer is affirmative.  The procedure \\(\\mathsf{VPA}\\) terminates with\nrational-nodal continuous piecewise-affine witnesses in \\(\\mathcal F_d\\) whose\n\\(A_d\\)-moments equal \\(m_d\\), and with rational outward enclosures of\n\\(U_d(m_d)\\) and \\(L_d(m_d)\\), each of width at most \\(\\epsilon\\).  Its\ncertificate checks exact continuous cell integrals, clipping, squared Euclidean\ngradient inequalities, a feasible atomic partial-transport plan, and the\ncontinuous remainder \\(M_dh(1+\\|\\lambda_d\\|_1)\\); no floating-residual or\nbit-complexity claim is made.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "S",
      "B",
      "mu_dj",
      "w",
      "nu",
      "d",
      "M_d",
      "m_d",
      "K_d",
      "r_d",
      "eps",
      "VPA",
      "F_d",
      "A_d",
      "U_d",
      "L_d",
      "h",
      "lambda_d"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:terminating-verified-reconstruction"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Apply the terminating verified-reconstruction theorem to the stated rational\ninput.  Its hypotheses are exactly the geometry, density, normalization,\ncompatibility, positive relative-interior radius, and finite rational tolerance\nlisted here.  That theorem constructs the required two primal witnesses and\nthe two rational endpoint enclosures, proves termination by dovetailed exact\nenumeration, and verifies each listed primal, transport, and continuous-remainder\ncondition.  Therefore it gives the affirmative answer verbatim.",
